IMPORTANT
This document records the proposed proprietary-use position for original Afghan AI materials. It is a draft notice, not proof of company registration, title to every component, or a signed agreement. It does not replace mandatory rights or exceptions under applicable law. The effective date, governing law, jurisdiction, company registration details, and any permitted user licence must be completed following legal review.

1. OWNERSHIP AND RIGHTS
Afghan AI is an educational technology project intended to support students and teachers through AI-assisted learning and educational services.

The proposed Licensor claims rights only in original software code, original designs, documentation, branding, and other proprietary materials that it lawfully owns or controls and that were developed specifically for Afghan AI. The founder is identified as the founder of the project; that designation alone does not establish ownership of every component or third-party resource used in the platform.

2. RESTRICTIONS ON UNAUTHORIZED USE
Except where expressly permitted in writing by the rights holder or allowed by applicable law, no person or organization may:
- Copy, redistribute, sell, sublicense, or commercially exploit protected Afghan AI materials.
- Modify, reproduce, or republish protected portions of the project's source code.
- Use protected branding, logos, or project materials in a way that falsely implies authorization or affiliation.
- Claim ownership of original Afghan AI materials owned by the rights holder.
- Remove applicable copyright notices from authorized copies of protected materials.

3. COMMERCIAL USE AND AUTHORIZATION
Commercial deployment, redistribution, licensing, or transfer of rights in materials owned by the rights holder requires prior written authorization, except where applicable law provides otherwise. Any approved use may be subject to a separate written agreement specifying scope, duration, territory, fees, and other conditions.

4. THIRD-PARTY MATERIALS AND AI SERVICES
This notice does not claim ownership of third-party software, open-source components, AI models, APIs, educational curricula, or other materials owned by others. Such components remain subject to their respective owners' rights, terms of service, and applicable licences. Their use does not transfer their ownership to the proposed Licensor.

5. NO AUTOMATIC TRANSFER OF RIGHTS
Access to the Afghan AI platform does not automatically grant ownership of its proprietary software, branding, or other protected materials. Any transfer or assignment of intellectual property rights must be documented in a separate written agreement executed by the relevant rights holders.

6. ENFORCEMENT AND LEGAL REMEDIES
The rights holder reserves any remedies available under applicable law for unauthorized use of intellectual property that it lawfully owns or controls. Nothing in this draft guarantees a particular legal outcome or overrides mandatory legal rights and exceptions.

